# Button groups

`Status: Draft` · `Owner: [name]`

Which Bootstrap button group combinations we use, and how. For deciding which action gets emphasis, see button hierarchy. For variants and themes, see buttons.

## TL;DR

- A button group is **two or three related actions**, joined, all the same variant.
- Four or more actions → show fewer and move the rest to an overflow menu.
- Never all-primary. Never mixed variants.
- Not for switching views, not for selecting a value, not for navigation.

## What it is

Two or three closely related actions presented as one joined control. Bootstrap's `.btn-group`.

The joining is the meaning: it says these actions belong together and apply to the same thing.

A row of buttons with gaps between them is **not** a button group — that is a cluster of separate actions, and button hierarchy covers it.

## When to use / when not to

| Situation | Use |
|---|---|
| Two or three actions on the same object | Button group |
| Four or more actions on the same object | One or two visible, rest in an overflow menu |
| Actions with no relationship to each other | Separate buttons, not a group |
| Variants of one action (Save / Save and new) | Split button |
| Switching between views of the same content | Not a button group. See Unresolved |
| Switching between different content sets | Tabs |
| A yes/no or on/off choice | Switch or checkbox. See forms |
| Choosing one value from a set | Radio group |
| Navigating somewhere | Links |

**Rules**

- A button group MUST contain only actions that apply to the same object or data.
- A button group MUST NOT be used to indicate a selection or a current state.
- A button group MUST NOT be used as navigation or as a substitute for tabs.
- Where actions are not related, they MUST be separated rather than grouped. Grouping unrelated actions implies a relationship that isn't there.
- A button group MUST NOT mix destructive and non-destructive actions. The proximity invites mistakes. See destructive actions.

## Styling

**One variant per group.**

A joined control reads as a single object. Mixing variants inside it breaks that reading — the shared border says these are peers, while a different fill says one of them matters more.

- Every button in a group MUST use the same variant and theme.
- Button groups use `btn-outline theme-secondary`.
- A button group MUST NOT contain a `btn-solid` button of any theme.
- A button group MUST NOT contain more than one visually distinct button.
- Where one action deserves more weight than the others, it MUST sit outside the group as a separate button. It does not belong inside a joined control.
- `btn-text` MUST NOT be used inside a button group. A borderless button inside a bordered group looks broken.

**Sizes**

- Every button in a group MUST be the same size.
- Groups use small or extra small. See buttons.

**Labels and icons**

- A group MUST NOT mix text-labelled buttons with icon-only buttons.
- **Exception:** a text-labelled button MAY be paired with an icon-only dropdown trigger belonging to it. That is a split button.
- Where every button in a group is icon-only, each MUST have an accessible name and a tooltip on hover and keyboard focus.
- Labels MUST be short and describe the action.

## How many

- Two or three actions. That is the whole range.
- At four or more, keep the most frequent one or two visible and move the rest to an overflow menu.
- A screen that needs many actions on the same object is a hierarchy problem, not a grouping problem. Lower the emphasis rather than adding buttons. See button hierarchy.

## Orientation

- Groups are horizontal by default.
- Vertical stacking is only for narrow layouts where horizontal does not fit.
- Below the tablet breakpoint, a group that does not fit MUST stack rather than scroll or truncate.

## Accessibility

- The group container MUST have `role="group"`, or `role="toolbar"` where it is a toolbar, with an `aria-label` naming what the group does.
- Buttons MUST be `<button type="button">`. An `<a>` is a link and a `<span>` is not announced as a button.
- Every button MUST be reachable by keyboard in visual order.
- Focus MUST be visible on each button in the group, including where borders are shared.

## Do this / not this

**Variant**
✅ Three `btn-outline theme-secondary` buttons, joined
❌ Four solid primary buttons in a row

**Count**
✅ `Message` · `Release profiles` · overflow menu containing the rest
❌ Six actions in one group

**Mixing**
✅ `Generate file ▾` — one text button with a dropdown trigger
❌ `Generate file` followed by two unlabelled icon buttons

**Wrong tool**
✅ Tabs for Videos / Pictures / Documents
❌ A button group for the same

